      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence fully describes how Ngram language models are used to predict/rank humorous statements. Chunk c-42b2a8b4190d48e2271bf4e7 explains the approach: models assign a probability to each input, enabling relative ranking. Two corpora are used (funny @midnight tweets and news data); tweets with higher probability under the funny-tweet model are considered funnier, while tweets with lower probability under the news model are viewed as funnier. Bigrams and trigrams are used as features with KenLM, modified Kneser-Ney smoothing, and back-off. This directly answers the question."
      },
      "elapsed_ms": 4701.95659995079
    },
    {
      "stage": "Generate",
      "attempt": 1,
